    {
      "id": "h67swm0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.6 Transactions and ACID Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Primary Keys cannot accept NULL values, whereas Unique Keys permit a single NULL value.",
        "DDL commands (CREATE, ALTER, DROP, TRUNCATE) are auto-committed, while DML commands (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE) require explicit COMMIT or ROLLBACK.",
        "Boyce-Codd Normal Form (BCNF) is a stricter variant of 3NF where every determinant functional dependency must be a Super Key.",
        "Concurrency control techniques like Two-Phase Locking (2PL) prevent conflict anomalies such as Dirty Reads and Lost Updates."
      ],
      "id": "dehcz9u"
    },
